        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rickjonzz/{size}/1934_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-10-12T15:48:34.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I had this idea listening to the live play. I like the way initiative passes works except that it seems to boil down to: all of the heroes but one go, then the villains go, then the last hero.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>What if one side couldn’t take more sequential turns than the other side?</p>\n<p>For example, the Freedom Five are fighting Citizen Dawn and 4 citizens.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The heroes go first. &nbsp;If they do the standard tactic then it’s 4 of them, then all of the bad guys plus the environment, then the last hero.</p>\n<p>But suppose Legacy goes, then Wraith then passes to Dawn. So at most, 2 villains can act before she has to pass back to the heroes. That feels like it might allow for a little more back and forth in combat. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>Thoughts?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:03.274Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
