        "id": 223114,
        "name": "VGBM",
        "username": "VGBM",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/vgbm/{size}/2020_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-10-12T17:37:40.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Cool idea. I'm not sure how well it'll work, but it's still neat.</p>\n<p>Personally, if I gm a game and I find my players doing the \"all but one\" technique, I'll just counter by doing the same thing in reverse order.</p>\n<p>So, say there's four heroes, a set of minions, a villain, and an environment turn, and the three of the four heroes went and then passed it to the minions. I'd have the minions pass to the remaining hero, forcing the villain and environment to go last, then on the start of the next round pass it back to each other giving me that (mostly) double villain turn they were trying to avoid.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:56:11.586Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
