        "raw": "<p>I think it all depends on how much of a jerk you, the GM, wish to be. Because the potential for jerk initiative in this system is high.</p>\r\n<p>I mean, tell your players about double villain turns ahead of time, and go ahead and take those double turns when the players hand them to you. But it's easy to do things like always pass to the Galvanizer at the top of the new round, just to make sure the bonus wear off. If you constantly do that, it's not gonna be much fun for that player, at the very least. Remember, you're not trying to&nbsp;<em>win</em>, you're trying to tell a story, and if a good story is told,&nbsp;<em>everyone</em> wins. :D</p>",
