      {
        "id": 223117,
        "name": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "username": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-10-13T00:42:18.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Reposting from another thread, re: the Initiative system:</p>\n<p>To me, that's an easy fix:</p>\n<p>1) The environment/scene tracker always goes last in initiative order.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>2) The environment does not get to 'choose' who goes next; the last player (or GM) to take a turn chooses who starts the next round (following the Environment/Scene Tracker).</p>\n<p>3) The GM may not pass initiative to themselves, even if they have multiple actors within the scene, unless all players have already gone.</p>\n<p>4) Any player who chooses to pass initiative to the GM may, on their next turn, reroll a single die of their choice.</p>\n<p>Yes, this doesn't \"eliminate\" the possibility of the players all going before the villain, but it does disincentivize doing so, as a player can reap a tangible, in-game benefit by passing play to the GM.&nbsp; Further, it makes GM tracking easier, by keeping the scene tracker's place in initiative static.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:56:11.801Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
