        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/aramis/{size}/1871_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-11-22T11:18:28.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I've been thinking about the same issue.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I've several conflicting ideas, and haven't tested a one....</p>\n<p>Idea 1:&nbsp; each side figures at start of encounter the consecutive action limit: 1+(Them/Us), round up. (THis sets a minimum of 2). Once a side is out, the other can run itself out.</p>\n<p>Idea 2: Larger side limited to 3 in a row, smaller to 2 in a row.</p>\n<p>idea 3: have an initial intiative roll, and generate a track like FFG's Star Wars does - who uses which slot for their side is open, but the slots themselves stay fixed. (The issue being that, unlike FFG SW, SCRPG adds new foes rather steadily...)</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
